## Build Cycle Summary

**Project:** Python CLI todo tool (`todo-cli`)
**PR:** https://github.com/mihirathale98/e2e-iter-todo/pull/1

**What was built:**
- 3-layer architecture: Typer CLI → Service layer → SQLite database
- 5 commands: `add`, `list`, `complete`, `delete`, `show`
- Rich colored tables with priority color-coding (high=red, medium=yellow, low=green)
- Natural language date parsing: `today`, `tomorrow`, `+3d`, `+1w`, ISO format
- SQLite single-file storage with parameterized queries

**Quality results:**
- 55 tests passing, ruff clean, mypy clean
- Eval composite score: 1.0
- Code review: CLEAN (7/7 categories PASS)
- Adversarial QA: 10/10 scenarios PASS with evidence
- 6 commits, 16 files, 1,129 lines

**Tech stack:** `typer[all]` as sole production dependency (includes Rich), sqlite3 + datetime + pathlib from stdlib

**Next steps:** PR #1 is open for human review and merge. Deferred items (PyPI publishing, recurring tasks, tags, cloud sync) documented in `.factory/strategy/deferred.md`.
